===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|chemistry}} A [[covalent bond]] (or series of bonds) between adjacent chains of a [[polymer]]
# {{lb|en|biochemistry}} A similar bond between [[strand]]s of [[nucleic acid]]
# {{lb|en|Internet}} An internal [[hyperlink]] to another [[webpage]] belonging to the same web [[domain name|domain]].
#: {{hypernyms|en|hyperlink}}
#: {{cot|en|backlink|alt1=back-link}}
#* {{quote-book|en|date=23-05-2006|title=Search Engine Optimization|author=Harold Davis|publisher=O’Reilly Media, Inc.|page=33|isbn=9781491905883|url= https://books.google.com/books?id=EbhSiSvzQLEC&pg=PA33|passage=There's no downside to providing reasonable '''cross links''', and several reasons for providing them.  For example, effective cross-linking keeps visitors on your site longer (as opposed to heading off-site because they can't find what they need on your site."}}
# {{lb|en|loosely}} A [[connection]] between [[data]].
#* {{quote-book|en|date=2021-12-11|url=https://op.europa.eu/en/publication-detail/-/publication/7a456b5b-5358-11ec-91ac-01aa75ed71a1|title=Proposal for a REGULATION OF THE EUROPEAN PARLIAMENT AND OF THE COUNCIL amending Regulation (EU) 2018/1727 of the European Parliament and the Council and Council Decision 2005/671/JHA, as regards the digital information exchange in terrorism cases |section=COM(2021) 757 final, 2021/0393(COD), recitals 9–14|passage=(12)For the identification of '''cross-links''' between terrorism investigations and judicial proceedings against suspects of terrorist offences, reliable identification data is crucial. Due to the uncertainties regarding alphanumerical data especially for third country nationals, it should be possible to exchange biometric data. Due to the sensitive nature of biometric data and the impact processing of biometric data has on the respect for private and family life and the protection of personal data, as enshrined in Articles 7 and 8 of the Charter of Fundamental Rights of the European Union, a strict necessity test should be applied by the competent authorities and Eurojust in each case.<br/><br/>(13)As information about existing '''cross-links''' to other judicial proceedings is most useful at an early stage of the investigation, it is necessary that the competent authorities provide information to Eurojust as soon as judicial authorities are involved. If the competent national authorities are already aware of '''cross-links''', they should inform Eurojust accordingly.}}

